<section image-layout="blank" id="TCTK_0ycka"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="lny8p3dvzs"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative worked example</p><h2>Not a brainstorm. A bounded bet.</h2><p font-size="lg">The question sets the boundary; the boundary makes the evidence interpretable.</p><spacer mode="fixed" size="14pt"/><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="cwekr6Po4x" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="17"><p role="eyebrow">1 · Question</p><h3>Can a six-word brief produce usable surprise?</h3><p role="caption">Name what the experiment must teach.</p></grid-item><grid-item vertical-align="center" colspan="4"><p font-size="32pt" align="center"><span text-color="accent">→</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="yrxTHSLz0R" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="18"><p role="eyebrow">2 · Test boundary</p><h4>Constants</h4><p>Monochrome · 30 minutes</p><hr color="neutral-border"/><h4>Variable</h4><p>One changed rule per round</p></grid-item><grid-item vertical-align="center" colspan="4"><p font-size="32pt" align="center"><span text-color="accent">→</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="XNSW_t6cDE" cell-style="subtle" cell-decor="side-line" colspan="17"><p role="eyebrow">3 · Decision gate</p><h4>Signal</h4><p>Surprising and usable from at least two of three reviewers.</p><hr color="neutral-border"/><h4>Stop</h4><p>After four rounds and 24 departures.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fixed" size="16pt"/><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h4>A bounded bet changes one variable while the question, evidence, and decision stay visible.</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>